<div class="trainer"><div class="fall" id="fall"><canvas id="fallCanvas"></canvas><div class="banner" id="banner">Press <b>Listen</b>, then play one real piano note.</div></div><div class="viewport" id="viewport"><div class="keyboard" id="keyboard"></div></div></div>
<div class="body"><div class="controls"><button class="primary" id="play">▶ Play demo</button><button id="stop">■ Stop</button><button class="listen" id="listen">🎤 Listen</button><button id="center">Center heard note</button><span class="pill">A4 <b id="a4top">440</b> Hz</span></div><p class="help">The lesson note is <b style="color:var(--target)">orange</b>. The note heard from the microphone is <b style="color:var(--heard)">blue</b>. When they are the same, the key turns <b style="color:var(--match)">green</b>. Microphone audio is analysed locally in the browser and is not uploaded by this app.</p></div></section>
<aside class="card"><div class="head"><h2>Live listener</h2></div><div class="body"><div class="readout">
<div class="metric"><div class="l">Heard note</div><div class="v" id="heardNote">—</div><div class="s" id="midi">Waiting</div></div><div class="metric"><div class="l">Frequency</div><div class="v" id="freq">—</div><div class="s">Hz</div></div><div class="metric"><div class="l">Tuning</div><div class="v" id="cents">—</div><div class="s">cents</div></div><div class="metric"><div class="l">Lesson</div><div class="v" id="match">—</div><div class="s" id="targetLabel">No target</div></div></div>
