<p class="small">For the first version, play one note at a time. Keep the device roughly 30–100 cm from the piano and reduce background noise. Chord/polyphonic recognition is a later feature.</p>
<details><summary>How it works</summary><p class="help">The browser reads the microphone waveform, downsamples it, estimates the repeating period with a YIN-style pitch detector, converts the frequency to the nearest MIDI piano note, and requires the same answer across several measurements before lighting a key.</p></details><details><summary>Known limitations</summary><p class="help">Real piano sounds contain harmonics, echoes and a noisy attack. A microphone pitch detector can occasionally jump to a harmonic or the wrong octave. Bass notes also need a longer listening window because their wave cycles are longer.</p></details></div><div class="head"><h3>Diagnostic log</h3><div class="spacer"></div><button id="clear">Clear</button></div><div class="body"><div class="log" id="log"></div></div></aside>
</div></main>
